    "answer": {
      "short": "Mary is correct: $\\sqrt{1-\\cos^2\\theta}=|\\sin\\theta|$, since $\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{1-\\cos^2\\theta}&=\\sqrt{\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\\\sqrt{1-\\cos^2\\theta}&=|\\sin\\theta|\\end{align*}$$\n\nMary is correct. The principal square root is nonnegative, whereas $\\sin\\theta$ can be negative. Bob's final equality holds only when $\\sin\\theta\\geq 0$.",
